IMPORT prelude

-- Electricity Act 2001 (Singapore) -- my supply and my premises: whether I need a licence for what I do with
-- electricity, when my supply may be cut off and must be put back, and what the electricity licensees may do on my land.
--
-- SEAT: the individual occupier of premises supplied with electricity -- the householder or other consumer -- who may
-- also own the premises, put up solar panels, sell electricity, or find a licensee's workers at the door.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 2 ("consumer", "contestable consumer", "electrical installation" as it bears on what I use),
-- s 6 with s 8 (activities that need an electricity licence) and s 6(2) (the fine), s 67 with s 71 and s 83(4) (the
-- installation licence for what I use), s 21(3) and s 26(2) (supply while my dispute is decided), s 23 (security),
-- s 24(1), (2), (4) and (5) (disconnection for an unpaid account, and reconnection), s 31(5), (7) to (12) (the
-- licensee's works on my land), s 32(3) to (6) (my trees), ss 33 to 36 and 77 (who can insist on entering my premises),
-- s 38 (the licensee's meter is not mine and cannot be taken for my debts), s 39 (emergency cut-off), and s 41(3) to (7)
-- (how I buy electricity once I am a contestable consumer).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 1/9/2025, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/EA2001.txt, with amendments to Act 27 of 2024 (in force 1 July 2025) shown.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the licensing procedure and licence conditions (ss 7, 9 to 20B), tariffs (s 22, whose figures are set by
-- the licensee and are not in the Act), s 25 (additional terms of supply), fuel stocks (s 27), special administration
-- (Part 4), control of licensees (Part 4A), rationing (Part 5A), gas (Part 5B), the wholesale market (Part 6),
-- competition (Part 7), the Appeal Panel (Part 8), s 37 (relocation, at the licensee's discretion), s 98 (appeal to
-- the Minister), and the machinery (administration, regulation-making, commencement). No exemption order under s 8 or
-- notification under s 71 is deposited, so whether one covers me is a fact I state.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual occupier, with the design
-- defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. It is not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Electricity Act 2001 -- my supply and my premises`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    Me
    `the market support services licensee`
    `the transmission licensee`

§§ `6 and 8 -- do I need an electricity licence for what I do`

-- s 6(1): "No person may -- (a) engage in the generation of electricity; (b) engage in the transmission of electricity;
-- (c) transmit electricity for or on behalf of a transmission licensee (other than as an employee of the transmission
-- licensee); (d) engage in the retail of electricity; (e) import or export electricity; (f) provide any market support
-- services; (g) trade in any wholesale electricity market; (h) operate any wholesale electricity market; or (i) [an
-- activity the Minister specifies] unless the person is authorised to do so by an electricity licence granted under
-- section 9 or is exempted under section 8."
-- s 2: "generate" means "to produce electricity by means of a generating station for the purpose of giving a supply to
-- any premises or enabling a supply to be so given"; "retail" means "to sell or offer to sell electricity to a
-- contestable consumer". Producing electricity for my own premises is "giving a supply to any premises" on the words;
-- that solar panels on my roof are therefore "generation" is an inference, not a holding.
-- s 6(1A) relieves only the Authority, which is never the person in this seat, so it is not encoded.
-- s 8(1): the Authority may "by order in the Gazette, exempt any person or class of persons". No order is deposited:
-- whether one covers me is a fact I state.
DECLARE `What I do with electricity` IS ONE OF
    `use electricity supplied to my premises`
    `produce electricity to supply premises, my own included`
    `sell or offer to sell electricity to a contestable consumer`
    `transmit electricity for a transmission licensee as its employee`
    `transmit electricity for a transmission licensee, not as its employee`
    `import or export electricity`
    `trade in a wholesale electricity market`

DECLARE `Licence answer` IS ONE OF
    `no licence is needed: section 6(1) does not list what I do`
    `I am covered: I hold an electricity licence for it`
    `I am covered: an exemption order under section 8 covers me`
    `I need an electricity licence: without one this is an offence under section 6(2)`

GIVEN `what I do` IS A `What I do with electricity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 6(1) list what I do` IF
    CONSIDER `what I do`
    WHEN `use electricity supplied to my premises` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `transmit electricity for a transmission licensee as its employee` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `what I do`                                    IS A `What I do with electricity`
      `I hold an electricity licence for it`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `an exemption order under section 8 covers me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Licence answer`
DECIDE `Do I need an electricity licence for what I do` IS
    BRANCH IF NOT `Does section 6(1) list what I do` `what I do`
              THEN `no licence is needed: section 6(1) does not list what I do`
           IF `I hold an electricity licence for it`
              THEN `I am covered: I hold an electricity licence for it`
           IF `an exemption order under section 8 covers me`
              THEN `I am covered: an exemption order under section 8 covers me`
           OTHERWISE `I need an electricity licence: without one this is an offence under section 6(2)`

-- s 6(2): "a fine not exceeding $500,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding
-- $12,500 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction". No imprisonment.
GIVEN `days or part days the offence continues after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be fined for an unlicensed activity` MEANS
    500000 PLUS 12500 TIMES `days or part days the offence continues after conviction`

§§ `2, 67, 71 and 83(4) -- do I need an installation licence for what I use`

-- s 67(1): "No person may -- (a) use, work or operate or permit to be used, worked or operated any electrical or supply
-- installation ... except under and in accordance with the terms of an electrical or a supply installation licence".
-- s 2: "electrical installation" means any appliance, wire, fitting or other apparatus placed in, on, over or under
-- any premises and used for the conveyance, control or use of electricity, "and includes a supply installation", but
-- does not include "(b) any appliance, wire, fitting or apparatus connected to and beyond any electrical outlet ... at
-- which fixed wiring terminates" or "(d) an electric vehicle charger within the meaning of the Electric Vehicles
-- Charging Act 2022". "supply installation": plant or apparatus "for the provision of electricity ... solely for the
-- person's own use".
-- s 71: the Authority "may, by notification in the Gazette, exempt ... (b) any electrical or supply installation used
-- exclusively for domestic purposes". No notification is deposited: whether one exempts mine is a fact I state.
-- s 83(4): contravening s 67(1) is punishable by "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding 3 years or ... both" and $250 a day (see the table in ea-offences.l4).
DECLARE `What I use` IS ONE OF
    `the fixed wiring, switches and sockets of my premises`
    `an appliance plugged into a socket`
    `an electric vehicle charger`
    `a generator or other plant supplying electricity solely for my own use`

GIVEN `what I use` IS A `What I use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I use an electrical installation` IF
    CONSIDER `what I use`
    WHEN `an appliance plugged into a socket` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an electric vehicle charger` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `what I use`                                          IS A `What I use`
      `I hold an electrical or supply installation licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notification under section 71 exempts it`          IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my use of it an offence under section 83(4)` IF
        `Is what I use an electrical installation` `what I use`
    AND NOT `I hold an electrical or supply installation licence`
    AND NOT `a notification under section 71 exempts it`

§§ `23 -- security for my supply`

-- s 23(3): where security has not been given or has become invalid or insufficient, "(a) the market support services
-- licensee or the transmission licensee may by notice require that person, within 7 days after the service of the
-- notice, to give it reasonable security ...; and (b) if that person fails to give such security, [it] may if it thinks
-- fit discontinue the supply of electricity for so long as the failure continues."
DECLARE `Supply action` IS ONE OF
    `give reasonable security for the money that may become due for my supply`
    `discontinue my supply for so long as the failure continues`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Supply action`
`my duty to give security after a section 23(3) notice` MEANS
    PARTY Me
    MUST  `give reasonable security for the money that may become due for my supply`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  PARTY `the market support services licensee`
          MAY   `discontinue my supply for so long as the failure continues`

§§ `24 -- may my supply be cut off for an unpaid account, and must it be put back`

-- s 24(1): if a market support services licensee "has good cause to direct a transmission licensee to disconnect a
-- non-contestable consumer ..., including the failure of the consumer to pay an account", it may so direct.
-- s 24(2): it "must not direct ... disconnect the supply of electricity to any residential premises by reason of failure
-- by the consumer to pay an account for that supply if the failure occurs through lack of sufficient income of the
-- consumer and of any other person normally resident on the premises supplied until -- (a) [it] has offered to advise
-- the consumer about optional methods of arranging payment of the account; and (b) the consumer -- (i) refuses or fails
-- to accept that offer of advice within the period (being not less than 7 days) specified ...; or (ii) accepts the offer
-- of advice, but refuses or fails to take any reasonable action to pay the account within the period (being not less
-- than 7 days) specified".
-- s 24(4): if a contestable consumer has not, on the due date, paid all charges due "to a transmission licensee", the
-- licensee may disconnect, discontinue the supply, and "recover any expenses incurred in so doing".
-- s 2: "contestable consumer" -- a consumer who buys from a retail electricity licensee or a wholesale market;
-- "non-contestable consumer" -- any other consumer. Which I am is set by regulations under s 41(1), not deposited, so
-- it is a fact I state.
DECLARE `My unpaid account` HAS
    `I am a contestable consumer`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the premises are residential`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 24(2): the hardship ground, "lack of sufficient income of the consumer and of any other person normally resident"
    `I failed to pay through lack of sufficient income of my household`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the licensee offered to advise me about optional methods of arranging payment`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the period the licensee gave me, in days`                                        IS A NUMBER
    `I did not accept the offer of advice within that period`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `I accepted the advice but took no reasonable action to pay within that period`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the period has run`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the unpaid charges are due to a transmission licensee`                           IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Disconnection answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: section 24(1) allows it, failure to pay being good cause`
    `not yet: section 24(2) protects me until the offer of advice and a period of at least 7 days have run`
    `yes: section 24(4) allows the transmission licensee to disconnect me and recover its expenses`
    `not covered by this encoding: section 24 does not deal with charges a contestable consumer owes a retailer`

GIVEN `the account` IS A `My unpaid account`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the section 24(2) protection run out` IF
        `the account`'s `the licensee offered to advise me about optional methods of arranging payment`
    AND `the account`'s `the period the licensee gave me, in days` AT LEAST 7
    AND `the account`'s `the period has run`
    AND (   `the account`'s `I did not accept the offer of advice within that period`
         OR `the account`'s `I accepted the advice but took no reasonable action to pay within that period`)

GIVEN `the account` IS A `My unpaid account`
GIVETH A `Disconnection answer`
DECIDE `May my supply be cut off for my unpaid account` IS
    BRANCH IF `the account`'s `I am a contestable consumer`
              THEN IF `the account`'s `the unpaid charges are due to a transmission licensee`
                      THEN `yes: section 24(4) allows the transmission licensee to disconnect me and recover its expenses`
                      ELSE `not covered by this encoding: section 24 does not deal with charges a contestable consumer owes a retailer`
           IF     `the account`'s `the premises are residential`
              AND `the account`'s `I failed to pay through lack of sufficient income of my household`
              AND NOT `Has the section 24(2) protection run out` `the account`
              THEN `not yet: section 24(2) protects me until the offer of advice and a period of at least 7 days have run`
           OTHERWISE `yes: section 24(1) allows it, failure to pay being good cause`

-- s 24(5): where the transmission licensee has disconnected for my default, it "must, subject to the market rules,
-- reconnect the supply ... within a reasonable time if the consumer in default has -- (a) made good the default;
-- (b) paid the reasonable expenses of disconnecting and re-connecting the supply; and (c) given such security as the
-- transmission licensee may reasonably require." The market rules are not deposited.
GIVEN `I have made good the default`                              IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have paid the reasonable expenses of disconnecting and reconnecting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have given the security the licensee reasonably requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my supply be reconnected within a reasonable time` IF
        `I have made good the default`
    AND `I have paid the reasonable expenses of disconnecting and reconnecting`
    AND `I have given the security the licensee reasonably requires`

§§ `21(3) and 26 -- must I be supplied while my dispute is decided`

-- s 26(1): a dispute "as to whether supply of electricity should be provided to that consumer" may be referred to the
-- Authority by either party, "whose decision is final and conclusive". (2): "the licensee must, subject to sections
-- 21(3) and 41(13), supply electricity to the consumer until the dispute is determined".
-- s 21(3) and s 41(13): no duty to procure supply if "(a) it is prevented from doing so by circumstances not within its
-- control; (b) [doing so would involve a licensee in a breach of this Act, despite all reasonable steps]; or (c) any
-- building on the premises has been erected in contravention of any written law or is in a ruinous or dangerous
-- condition." Whether (a) or (b) holds is the licensee's case to make; it is asked as one fact.
GIVEN `my dispute about supply has been referred to the Authority`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority has determined it`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
      `circumstances outside the licensee's control prevent supply, or supplying would put a licensee in breach` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a building on my premises was put up unlawfully or is ruinous or dangerous` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be supplied until my dispute is determined` IF
        `my dispute about supply has been referred to the Authority`
    AND NOT `the Authority has determined it`
    AND NOT `circumstances outside the licensee's control prevent supply, or supplying would put a licensee in breach`
    AND NOT `a building on my premises was put up unlawfully or is ruinous or dangerous`

§§ `31 -- may the licensee enter my land to do its works`

-- s 31(7): "Except in the case of an emergency arising from any fault in any electric line or electrical plant, the
-- licensee ... must, before entering any land ..., give 14 days' written notice to the owner or occupier".
-- (9): "The owner or occupier ... may, within 14 days of the receipt of the notice ..., lodge a written objection with
-- the Authority". (10): "If no objection is lodged within the period ..., the licensee may enter on the land and do all
-- or any of the works specified in the notice." (11), (12): an objection not withdrawn goes to an inquiry, after which
-- the Authority "may authorise" the works, unconditionally or on terms. (8): otherwise I "must comply with the notice
-- and do all things necessary to facilitate the carrying out of the work". (5): the licensee "must pay compensation to
-- any person who suffers any damage or loss of value to the person's property" in an amount agreed. (17): it pays no
-- fee for the right to enter.
-- The Authority's authorisation after an inquiry is a judgment handed to someone else: it is an input.
DECLARE `Works answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: an emergency from a fault, so no notice is needed`
    `not yet: it has not given me 14 days' written notice`
    `only if the Authority authorises the works after an inquiry into my objection`
    `yes: the Authority has authorised the works after the inquiry`
    `yes: I lodged no objection within 14 days, so I must facilitate the works`

GIVEN `there is an emergency arising from a fault in a line or plant`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `days since I received the licensee's written notice`               IS A NUMBER
      `I lodged a written objection with the Authority within 14 days`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `I withdrew my objection before the inquiry`                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority authorised the works after the inquiry`              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Works answer`
DECIDE `May the licensee enter my land to do the works in its notice` IS
    BRANCH IF `there is an emergency arising from a fault in a line or plant`
              THEN `yes: an emergency from a fault, so no notice is needed`
           IF `days since I received the licensee's written notice` LESS THAN 14
              THEN `not yet: it has not given me 14 days' written notice`
           IF `I lodged a written objection with the Authority within 14 days` AND NOT `I withdrew my objection before the inquiry`
              THEN IF `the Authority authorised the works after the inquiry`
                      THEN `yes: the Authority has authorised the works after the inquiry`
                      ELSE `only if the Authority authorises the works after an inquiry into my objection`
           OTHERWISE `yes: I lodged no objection within 14 days, so I must facilitate the works`

§§ `32 -- my trees near the licensee's lines`

-- s 32(3): where a tree felled or dealt with by the licensee "was in existence before the electricity licensee's
-- installation or plant was placed", the licensee "must ... pay to any person adversely affected such sum as may be
-- agreed ... or in the absence of agreement, such sum as may be determined by the Authority".
-- (4): no further compensation where the tree "has grown or has been allowed to grow since the payment of compensation".
-- (5): none for a tree "within 20 metres of the centre line of any road constructed or maintained by the Government or by
-- any public authority unless it is proved that the tree or vegetation was in existence prior to the construction of
-- the road".
GIVEN `the tree was there before the licensee's installation`                IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was paid compensation before and the tree has regrown since`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `metres from the centre line of a public road`                         IS A NUMBER
      `it is proved the tree was there before the road was built`            IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I owed compensation for my felled tree` IF
        `the tree was there before the licensee's installation`
    AND NOT `I was paid compensation before and the tree has regrown since`
    AND (   `metres from the centre line of a public road` GREATER THAN 20
         OR `it is proved the tree was there before the road was built`)

-- s 32(6): an owner or occupier who fells, lops or clears a tree "adjacent to an electricity licensee's installation or
-- plant ... must give the licensee 14 days' written notice" and take the reasonable precautions it requires. (7): if not,
-- the owner or occupier "is liable to pay the licensee any cost and expense ... for any damage caused". (8): a tree so
-- felled is "presumed until the contrary is proved" to have been felled by the owner or occupier or their agents.
GIVEN `days of written notice I gave the licensee before felling` IS A NUMBER
      `I took the precautions the licensee required`             IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I pay for damage my tree-felling caused the licensee's plant` IF
    `days of written notice I gave the licensee before felling` LESS THAN 14 OR (NOT `I took the precautions the licensee required`)

§§ `33 to 36 and 77 -- who can insist on entering my premises`

-- s 33(1), (2): a person authorised by a transmission or market support services licensee may enter "at any reasonable
-- time" to survey, but "must not demand to do so as of right unless -- (a) 7 days' notice of the intended entry has been
-- given to the occupier; and (b) if required to do so, the person has produced evidence of the person's authority."
-- s 34: while supply is being given, an authorised person may "at all reasonable times, on the production of some duly
-- authenticated document showing the person's authority, enter" to inspect the licensee's line or plant, read, remove
-- or replace the meter, or maintain the supply.
-- s 35(1): where the supply may be disconnected, or I cease to need it, an authorised person may enter "at all
-- reasonable hours, on production of some duly authenticated document" to disconnect or remove plant or the meter.
-- (2): "Subject to section 39, the person ... must not enter any dwelling house in actual occupation without 6 hours'
-- previous notice to the occupier, unless the occupier has given the occupier's consent to the entry."
-- s 36(1): to place new, or maintain, repair or alter existing, lines or plant, "after 7 days' notice to the occupier
-- ..., at all reasonable times, on production of some duly authenticated document". (2): in an emergency from a fault,
-- "entry may be made ... without the notice", given as soon as possible after.
-- s 77(1): an authorised officer of the Authority may enter premises with an installation "at all reasonable hours of the
-- day and at any time when the electrical or supply installation is in operation". (3): "No person is obliged to admit
-- into the person's premises any person purporting to be an authorised officer except upon production of such
-- identification card or badge."
-- s 88 (in ea-offences.l4): hindering or obstructing a licensee's employee, agent or contractor in what it is
-- authorised to do is an offence. That a lawful entry under these sections is such a thing is an inference.
DECLARE `Why they want to come in` IS ONE OF
    `to survey whether my premises suit the licensee's activities (s 33)`
    `to inspect the licensee's line or plant, read or change the meter, or maintain supply (s 34)`
    `to disconnect my supply or remove the licensee's plant or meter (s 35)`
    `to place, repair or alter the licensee's line or plant (s 36)`
    `to inspect an installation as an authorised officer of the Authority (s 77)`

DECLARE `A visit to my premises` HAS
    `why they want to come in`                                            IS A `Why they want to come in`
    `it is a reasonable time`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `they produced a document or card showing their authority`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours of notice I was given`                                         IS A NUMBER
    `there is an emergency arising from a fault in a line or plant`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the premises are a dwelling house I actually occupy`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `I consented to the entry`                                            IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the visit` IS A `A visit to my premises`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can this person insist on entering my premises` IF
    CONSIDER `the visit`'s `why they want to come in`
    WHEN `to survey whether my premises suit the licensee's activities (s 33)` THEN
            `the visit`'s `it is a reasonable time`
        AND `the visit`'s `hours of notice I was given` AT LEAST 168
        AND `the visit`'s `they produced a document or card showing their authority`
    WHEN `to inspect the licensee's line or plant, read or change the meter, or maintain supply (s 34)` THEN
            `the visit`'s `it is a reasonable time`
        AND `the visit`'s `they produced a document or card showing their authority`
    WHEN `to disconnect my supply or remove the licensee's plant or meter (s 35)` THEN
            `the visit`'s `it is a reasonable time`
        AND `the visit`'s `they produced a document or card showing their authority`
        AND (   NOT `the visit`'s `the premises are a dwelling house I actually occupy`
             OR `the visit`'s `hours of notice I was given` AT LEAST 6
             OR `the visit`'s `I consented to the entry`)
    WHEN `to place, repair or alter the licensee's line or plant (s 36)` THEN
            `the visit`'s `it is a reasonable time`
        AND `the visit`'s `they produced a document or card showing their authority`
        AND (   `the visit`'s `hours of notice I was given` AT LEAST 168
             OR `the visit`'s `there is an emergency arising from a fault in a line or plant`)
    WHEN `to inspect an installation as an authorised officer of the Authority (s 77)` THEN
            `the visit`'s `it is a reasonable time`
        AND `the visit`'s `they produced a document or card showing their authority`

-- s 33(2)(b) requires evidence of authority only "if required to do so"; the encoding treats my asking as requiring it,
-- and asks the fact as whether it was produced.

§§ `38 and 39 -- the licensee's equipment, and emergency cut-off`

-- s 38: any plant, line, meter or fitting "owned or let for hire or lent to a consumer by an electricity licensee" and
-- affixed to the premises "(a) continues to remain the property of that licensee and is deemed not to be a fixture, and
-- does not vest in the owner of the premises; and (b) is not to be subject to distress or be liable to be taken under or
-- pursuant to an enforcement order of any court or any proceedings in bankruptcy against the person in whose possession
-- it is." Whether equipment that is mine can be taken is for the law of enforcement and bankruptcy, not reached here.
GIVEN `the equipment is owned by, or let or lent to me by, an electricity licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 38 keep the equipment from being taken for my debts or in my bankruptcy` IF
    `the equipment is owned by, or let or lent to me by, an electricity licensee`

-- s 39(1): where a licensee "is of the opinion that immediate action is necessary" in an emergency, for public safety
-- or to avoid undue interference with supply to others, it "(a) may forthwith discontinue the supply ...; (b) must
-- immediately thereafter give written notice of the discontinuance to the person". (2): "An electricity licensee is not
-- liable for any loss or damage caused to any person by such discontinuance". Encoded as the licensee's power that
-- binds me, conditional on its opinion. Whether any claim would otherwise lie is outside the Act.
GIVEN `the licensee is of the opinion that immediate action is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 39 bar my claim for loss from an emergency cut-off` IF
    `the licensee is of the opinion that immediate action is necessary`

§§ `41 -- how I buy electricity once I am a contestable consumer`

-- s 41(5): "A consumer has the option to, within a period of 30 days from the date on which the consumer is classified
-- ... as a contestable consumer (or such further period as the Authority may determine) -- (a) commence purchasing
-- electricity under a contract with a retail electricity licensee; or (b) commence purchasing electricity directly from
-- any wholesale electricity market." (4): direct purchase only if "granted a licence by the Authority to do so and is
-- registered as a market participant". (7): "If a consumer does not commence purchasing ..., the consumer is deemed to
-- commence purchasing electricity indirectly from any wholesale electricity market through a market support services
-- licensee at prevailing market prices" from the day after the period. (9): I may change option at any time after.
-- (6), (8): an existing supply agreement ceases from the date the new option begins.
DECLARE `What I did after becoming contestable` IS ONE OF
    `nothing yet`
    `contracted with a retail electricity licensee`
    `began buying directly from a wholesale market, licensed and registered`

DECLARE `Purchase answer` IS ONE OF
    `from my retail electricity licensee, on the terms we agreed`
    `directly from the wholesale market at prevailing market prices`
    `still mine to choose: the 30-day period has not run`
    `deemed: indirectly from the wholesale market through the market support services licensee at prevailing market prices`

GIVEN `what I did`                                        IS A `What I did after becoming contestable`
      `days since I was classified as contestable`        IS A NUMBER
      `further days the Authority allowed`                IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Purchase answer`
DECIDE `How am I buying electricity as a contestable consumer` IS
    CONSIDER `what I did`
    WHEN `contracted with a retail electricity licensee` THEN `from my retail electricity licensee, on the terms we agreed`
    WHEN `began buying directly from a wholesale market, licensed and registered` THEN `directly from the wholesale market at prevailing market prices`
    WHEN `nothing yet` THEN
        IF `days since I was classified as contestable` GREATER THAN 30 PLUS `further days the Authority allowed`
